  "behavior": [
    "EVM and Substrate admission bind the mobile session topic, approved method/chain/account tuple, decoded identity, expiry, peer, namespaces and revision. Proposal namespaces cannot authorize signing and independent grants cannot be combined.",
    "Private session snapshots are detached from the live client and omitted from published review payloads. Current account/topic and session data are checked before forwarding and after transport returns.",
    "Session update/extend increment revisions. Delete/expire/disconnect retire topics synchronously, so unchanged or restored session records cannot revive earlier approvals. Provider initialization is shared and lifecycle listeners attach once per client.",
    "Forwarded parameters are detached and returned EVM message/typed signatures and Substrate signatures must match the private reviewed bytes before release. Remote transaction hash verification remains a separate gate.",
    "Raw Substrate requests use polkadot_signMessage with hex-encoded wrapped bytes. A stable approved chain carrying the same decoded account is selected only as transport routing; raw bytes do not claim chain binding. Native hex-verbatim signers and idempotently wrapping peers receive the same required signed bytes.",
    "Tab entry snapshots payloads before the authorization wait and supports mobile accounts without looking up a local pair. Stored public metadata is preserved. The internal mobile extrinsic adapter also captures account/metadata/session and verifies its returned signature."
  ],
